title: "The cortical column as a tuned receiver: a network mechanism for temporal-interference stimulation"
abstract: >-
  Weak-field cellular nonlinearities contribute to an effective quadratic
  mixing response in temporal-interference stimulation. Population models
  separate carrier access, difference-frequency generation, and recurrent amplification.
  Building on axonal rectification in single-neuron TI models, a short effective
  membrane time represents candidate fast access; its TI-field transfer requires calibration. The static transfer curve emerges from the exact QIF mean field in the
  slow-synapse limit; carrier mixing requires the corresponding separation of
  time scales. Near a Hopf bifurcation, the recurrent network amplifies the
  generated beat. Demonstrated with Jansen-Rit, NMM2, and QIF models, with a
  laminar extension and comparison with direct low-frequency stimulation.
type: software
